# --- Blocked: the test count --------------------------------------------------
#
# The README says nothing about the size of the suite, and adding "769 tests"
# would fail CHT-3: no committed artefact carries that number, and CHT-3 is the
# test that requires one. The two ways past it are both wrong.
#
#   - Put it in a fenced code block. CHT-3 strips those before extracting
#     numbers, so it would pass while checking nothing. That is gaming our own
#     guard in the README the guard exists to protect.
#   - Add "769" to STRUCTURAL in tests/test_charts.py, which is not on this
#     allowlist, and which would exempt a figure that is neither structural nor
#     stable.
#
# Left out and reported instead. The honest fix is for the suite to write its
# own count to an artefact, which is a code change on a documentation
# checkpoint.

# --- Reported, not fixed: out/ is not on this allowlist -----------------------
#
# out/metrics.json carries meta.checkpoint = "CP13.1" and contains HYBRID, which
# CP17 added. The artefact every README number traces to mislabels its own
# vintage. Regenerating it is a 10,000-case run and out/ is not allowlisted.
#
# CHT-3 checks existence, not derivation. "255x the contacts" is 9,192/36, and
# no field in metrics.json holds that ratio — it passes because 255 is B2's
# SF-4 count. The same is true of 2.34x and 3.5 points. The check catches
# invented numbers and does not catch a derived one that is wrong, and every
# such ratio in the README was re-derived by hand for this audit instead.
